Proves `qdet3_00_nc_eq_qdet3`: over a field $F$ with $A_{22} 
eq 0$ and $q = A_{11} - A_{12}(A_{22})^{-1}A_{21} 
eq 0$, the non-commutative definition equals the det-ratio definition. The proof is `field_simp; ring` after unfolding all definitions. The hypothesis $q 
eq 0$ is needed to interpret $q^{-1}$ as the field inverse (not a formal symbol).
